First, I started playing NH3.1 on my 20 Mhz 286 with a 2MB harddisk cash, and
it was *very* slow.  Then, I read the documentation that came with it which
indicated that you need every byte of the lower 640K available to get a speed
improvement.

So I bought DR DOS 6.0 and used its memory manager to move DOS into high
memory (my machine has a NEAT chipset which DR DOS knows about).  I went from
540Kb available to about 619Kb availble of the lower 640Kb.

This made all the difference!  I still can tell when a level has a shop or a
large number of monsters (like a ghost level), but otherwise it is reasonably
quick.

Read the nethack doc's.  They make it pretty clear the best way to speed on a
PC clone is to free up as much of the lower 640Kb as possible.

